 with 256MB of VRAM or ATI Radeon HD 2600 Pro with 256MB of VRAM"],["Sound","Direct X 9.0c compatible sound card"],["DirectX\u00ae","Direct X 9.0c"]],"rec":[["Processor","Quad Core running at 2.8 GHz or equivalent"],["Memory","2GB (Windows XP) or 3GB (Windows Vista/7)"],["Graphics","nVidia 8800 GT graphics card with 512MB of VRAM"]],"deck":2,"blurb":"Nazi-occupied Paris in the 1940s is the backdrop for The Saboteur, an open-world action game starring Sean Devlin, an Irish racecar mechanic who joins the French Resistance to get revenge on Colonel Kurt Dierker, the officer who executed his best friend. Missions mix gunfights, stealth, disguises and driving, with sabotage targets such as trains, bridges and enemy facilities, and landmarks like the Eiffel Tower and Notre Dame can be climbed.\n\nThe city's color is drained in areas under heavy occupation and returns as the Resistance regains ground, giving it a distinctive look. It is a single-player game suited to players who want pulpy, World War II-set open-world action rather than a realistic war simulation."}}